Fix \(\chi>1\).  For every \(0<\epsilon<10^{-3}\) and every \(B\ge5\chi\), the exact integer-budget CLW selector at \(P_{\chi,\epsilon}\) is \(\{d_{\mathrm p}\}\), whereas \(D^*(P_{\chi,\epsilon})=D_{\mathrm{IKM}}^*(P_{\chi,\epsilon})=\{d_{\mathrm e}\}\).  The eight center ratios
\[
 \rho_{\mathrm{CLW}},\quad
 \rho_{\mathrm{CLW}}^{\mathrm{int}},\quad
 \rho_{\mathrm{pred}},\quad
 \rho_{\mathrm{pred}}^A,
 \qquad
 \rho_{\mathrm{CLW}}^{\mathrm{IKM}},\quad
 \rho_{\mathrm{CLW}}^{\mathrm{IKM,int}},\quad
 \rho_{\mathrm{pred}}^{\mathrm{IKM}},\quad
 \rho_{\mathrm{pred}}^{A,\mathrm{IKM}}
\]
all equal
\[
 \rho_\chi(\epsilon)=\frac{25}{3872}
 \left\{
 \sqrt{\frac{20\chi(5\chi-1)}{10\chi-3}}
 +\sqrt{\frac{32(5\chi+1)}{75(10\chi-3)}
 (\epsilon^{-2}+14)}
 \right\}^{2}.                                             \tag{1}
\]
This common value exceeds \((\epsilon^{-2}+14)/726\) and, for fixed \(\chi\),
\[
 \rho_\chi(\epsilon)=
 \frac{5\chi+1}{363(10\chi-3)}\epsilon^{-2}
 +O_\chi(\epsilon^{-1}).                                  \tag{2}
\]
For every \(B\ge5\chi\), the suitably shrunk regions satisfy
\[
 \sup_{P\in\mathcal U_{\mathrm{bin}}}
 \rho_{\mathrm{CLW}}^{\mathrm{int}}(P;B)=\infty,
 \qquad
 \sup_{P\in\mathcal U_{\mathrm{bin}}^{\mathrm{IKM}}}
 \rho_{\mathrm{CLW}}^{\mathrm{IKM,int}}(P;B)=\infty.      \tag{3}
\]
The optimized integer envelope is understood with joint budget feasibility:
\[
 \inf_{\substack{\chi>1\\ B\ge5\chi}}
 \rho_{\mathrm{CLW}}^{\mathrm{int}}(P_{\chi,\epsilon};B)
 =\inf_{\substack{\chi>1\\ B\ge5\chi}}
 \rho_{\mathrm{CLW}}^{\mathrm{IKM,int}}(P_{\chi,\epsilon};B)
 =\inf_{\chi>1}\rho_\chi(\epsilon),                     \tag{4}
\]
and every minimizing \(\chi\) satisfies
\[
 \chi_{\mathrm{opt}}(\epsilon)
 \sim\frac{\sqrt[3]{18}}{15}\epsilon^{-2/3},
\]
\[
 \epsilon^2\inf_{\chi>1}\rho_\chi(\epsilon)
 =\frac1{726}+\frac{5\sqrt[3]{12}}{968}\epsilon^{2/3}
 +o(\epsilon^{2/3}).                                      \tag{5}
\]
Thus (5) applies along any budget schedule large enough to satisfy \(B_\epsilon\ge5\chi_{\mathrm{opt}}(\epsilon)\); it is not an unrestricted optimization over \(\chi\) at one fixed finite budget.  The named empirical counterpart is treated separately and no result concerns approximate OGA, an arbitrary predictive method, the original randomized-trial theorem, persistent-confounding analysis by Carneiro--Lee--Wilhelm, or bridge-role choice by that paper.

defs.def:binary-ikmw-region:
Fix the prescribed \(\chi>1\). For every \(0<\epsilon<10^{-3}\), choose the radius \(r_\epsilon^{\mathrm{IKM}}>0\) furnished by Lemma~\(\mathrm{lem{:}binary\text{-}ikmw\text{-}normalized\text{-}stability}\) after the joint shrinking permitted by Lemma~\(\mathrm{lem{:}joint\text{-}predictive\text{-}binary\text{-}stability}\), and let \(\delta_\epsilon\) be the radius used in Definition~\(\mathrm{def{:}binary\text{-}region}\). Choose
\[
 0<\widetilde\delta_\epsilon
 <\min\{\delta_\epsilon,r_\epsilon^{\mathrm{IKM}}\}
\]
and define
\[
 \mathcal U_{\mathrm{bin}}^{\mathrm{IKM}}
 =\bigcup_{0<\epsilon<10^{-3}}
 \left\{P\in\mathcal M_{\mathrm{bin}}(\chi):
 \|P-P_\epsilon\|_{\mathrm{cell}}<\widetilde\delta_\epsilon\right\}. \tag{1}
\]
Every member belongs to \(\mathfrak P_{\mathcal D}^{\mathrm{CLW}}\), and, for every \(B>0\), the strict continuous CLW selector, both generic unrestricted-risk selectors, and the strict IKM-normalized optimizer are stable throughout every displayed ball. The named IKM ratio \(\rho_{\mathrm{CLW}}^{\mathrm{IKM}}(P;B)\) and both generic IKM ratios each exceed one half of their corresponding center value after the stated shrinking. Thus \(\mathcal U_{\mathrm{bin}}^{\mathrm{IKM}}\subseteq\mathcal U_{\mathrm{bin}}\) and is relatively open in \(\mathcal M_{\mathrm{bin}}(\chi)\).

defs.def:observable-bridge-law-class:
\[
\mathfrak P_{\mathcal D}^{\mathrm{obs}}
=\left\{P:\begin{array}{l}
\text{source-arm positivity, a square-integrable observed outcome bridge, a square-integrable}\cr
\text{observed selection bridge, designwise bijectivity of \(T_d\), and finite strictly positive}\cr
\text{source-score variances hold for every \(d\in\mathcal D\)}
\end{array}\right\}.
\]

defs.def:binary-region:
Fix the prescribed \(\chi>1\). For every \(0<\epsilon<10^{-3}\), choose the radius \(r_\epsilon>0\) furnished by Lemma~\(\mathrm{lem{:}binary\text{-}witness\text{-}stability}\) after the joint shrinking permitted by Lemma~\(\mathrm{lem{:}joint\text{-}predictive\text{-}binary\text{-}stability}\), and set \(r_\epsilon^{\mathrm{opt}}:=r_\epsilon\). Choose \(0<\delta_\epsilon<r_\epsilon^{\mathrm{opt}}\) and define
\[
 \mathcal U_{\mathrm{bin}}
 =\bigcup_{0<\epsilon<10^{-3}}
 \left\{P\in\mathcal M_{\mathrm{bin}}(\chi):
 \|P-P_\epsilon\|_{\mathrm{cell}}<\delta_\epsilon\right\}. \tag{1}
\]
Every member belongs to \(\mathfrak P_{\mathcal D}\cap\mathfrak P_{\mathcal D}^{\mathrm{CLW}}\), has both bridge contrasts equal to \(\tau\), and, for every \(B>0\), retains the strict continuous CLW, unrestricted unadjusted-risk, unrestricted treatment-aware-risk, and arm-normalized source-score optimizer assignments furnished by the two stability lemmas. For every fixed \(P\) in (1), there is a finite \(B_0(P)\) such that the integer CLW selector has the same singleton value for all \(B\ge B_0(P)\). Thus \(\mathcal U_{\mathrm{bin}}\subseteq\mathfrak P_{\mathcal D}\) and is relatively open in \(\mathcal M_{\mathrm{bin}}(\chi)\). No claim of openness in the ambient unrestricted probability simplex is made, because the factorization, support, consistency, and causal equality restrictions define a lower-dimensional model.

defs.def:ikmw-normalized-design-value:
For each regular design \(d\), define
\[
 \psi_{E,d}^{\mathrm{IKM}}=(1-p_{E,1})\phi_{E,d},
 \qquad
 \psi_{O,d}^{\mathrm{IKM}}=(1-p_{O,1})\phi_{O,d},
\]
\[
 V_{E,d}^{\mathrm{IKM}}=(1-p_{E,1})^2V_{E,d},
 \qquad
 V_{O,d}^{\mathrm{IKM}}=(1-p_{O,1})^2V_{O,d}.             \tag{1}
\]
The profiled IKM-normalized value and its tie-preserving optimizer set are
\[
 \mathcal V_{d,\mathrm{IKM}}^*(P)
 =\left\{
 \sqrt{c_{E,d}V_{E,d}^{\mathrm{IKM}}}
 +\sqrt{c_{O,d}V_{O,d}^{\mathrm{IKM}}}
 \right\}^2,
 \qquad
 D_{\mathrm{IKM}}^*(P)
 =\arg\min_{d\in\mathcal D}\mathcal V_{d,\mathrm{IKM}}^*(P). \tag{2}
\]
The best-tie IKM ratios for the named continuous CLW selector and the two generic unrestricted-risk selectors are, respectively,
\[
 \rho_{\mathrm{CLW}}^{\mathrm{IKM}}(P;B)
 =\frac{\min_{d\in\mathcal D_{\mathrm{CLW}}(P;B)}
 \mathcal V_{d,\mathrm{IKM}}^*(P)}
 {\min_{d'\in\mathcal D}\mathcal V_{d',\mathrm{IKM}}^*(P)}, \tag{3}
\]
\[
 \rho_{\mathrm{pred}}^{\mathrm{IKM}}(P)
 =\frac{\min_{d\in\mathcal D_{\mathrm{pred}}(P)}
 \mathcal V_{d,\mathrm{IKM}}^*(P)}
 {\min_{d'\in\mathcal D}\mathcal V_{d',\mathrm{IKM}}^*(P)},
 \qquad
 \rho_{\mathrm{pred}}^{A,\mathrm{IKM}}(P)
 =\frac{\min_{d\in\mathcal D_{\mathrm{pred}}^A(P)}
 \mathcal V_{d,\mathrm{IKM}}^*(P)}
 {\min_{d'\in\mathcal D}\mathcal V_{d',\mathrm{IKM}}^*(P)}. \tag{4}
\]
These are normalization-specific source-score profiles. Their interpretation as causal efficiency bounds is supplied design by design only under Lemma~\(\mathrm{lem{:}ikmw\text{-}fixed\text{-}system\text{-}efficiency}\) after its causal-identification and regularity premises have been verified. The named selector in (3) transports only the CLW population affine-linear criterion; neither (3) nor (4) attributes persistent-confounding analysis or bridge-role selection to a published paper.

snapshot.stmt:
Fix \(\chi>1\), let \(\epsilon_m\in(0,10^{-3})\) satisfy \(\epsilon_m\downarrow0\), and suppose the independently funded full-catalogue pilot consists of independent and identically distributed draws from \(P_{\chi,\epsilon_m}\), independently of the main study.  Apply Definition~\(\mathrm{def{:}clw\text{-}empirical\text{-}linear\text{-}cost\text{-}selector}\).  Then
\[
 \max_{d\in\mathcal D}
 \left|\widehat r_{d,m}^{\mathrm{lin}}
 -r_d^{\mathrm{lin}}(P_{\chi,\epsilon_m})\right|
 =O_P(m^{-1/2}).                                           \tag{1}
\]
For every fixed \(B\ge5\chi\),
\[
 \max_{d\in\mathcal D}
 \left|\widehat\Psi_{\mathrm{CLW},d,m}^{\mathrm{int}}(B)
 -\Psi_{\mathrm{CLW},d}^{\mathrm{int}}(P_{\chi,\epsilon_m};B)\right|
 =O_P(m^{-1/2}),                                           \tag{2}
\]
with the analogous conclusion for the continuous criteria, and
\[
 P_{\chi,\epsilon_m}\!\left\{
 \widehat d_{\mathrm{CLW},m}(B)
 =\widehat d_{\mathrm{CLW},m}^{\mathrm{int}}(B)
 =d_{\mathrm p}\right\}\longrightarrow1.                \tag{3}
\]
Moreover,
\[
 \widehat\rho_{\mathrm{CLW},m}^{\mathrm{int}}
 (P_{\chi,\epsilon_m};B)\longrightarrow_P+\infty,
 \qquad
 \widehat\rho_{\mathrm{CLW},m}^{\mathrm{IKM,int}}
 (P_{\chi,\epsilon_m};B)\longrightarrow_P+\infty.       \tag{4}
\]
No rate relation between \(m\) and \(\epsilon_m\) is required.  The boundary \(B=5\chi\) is included.  No conclusion is asserted for \(B<5\chi\), where the prediction-selected design can have zero exact budget count, or at the singular limit \(\epsilon=0\).  This theorem analyzes the exact finite-catalogue affine least-squares minimizer corresponding to Carneiro--Lee--Wilhelm equation~(3.6), not their approximate OGA procedure.

